    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `fill_gaps` in `app/gaps.py`. The existing tests pass (2 passed), and a quick check of my own showed it fills gaps the way you described.\n\n**How it works:** it copies the input, then fills `temp_c` within each station. First it carries each station's last temperature forward to later reports. Any report still missing a value (one with no earlier temperature) then takes that station's first later temperature. Values never cross between stations, and all other columns are left as they were.\n\n**What I checked:**\n- **Sample data:** station A's first missing reading gets its later 11.0, B's missing reading gets its earlier 7.5, and the input frame is unchanged afterwards.\n- **Station with no temperatures:** it keeps its missing values.\n- **Row order and index:** both come back unchanged, even when index labels repeat.\n- **Rows with no station:** they keep their existing temperature and aren't filled, because there's no station to fill from.\n\nThere are still no tests for `fill_gaps` itself; the two existing tests only cover loading the data.\n\n**Leftover file:** my check script `scratch_check.py` is still in the project root. The shell needed your approval to delete it, so please remove it yourself or tell me to."
